WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.150
Winning over audiences with his joyfulness,
hyper-literal language, and sense of loyalty,

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.330
the interstellar warrior Drax the Destroyer
is one of the brightest figures in the Marvel

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:10.380
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.520
You couldn't quite say the same for his comic
book counterpart.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.480
In many ways, Dave Bautista's interpretation
of Drax is barely recognizable from the character

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.080
in the comics and for once, that's not a bad
thing.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:27.699
Since his debut in 1973's Iron Man #55, Drax
the Destroyer has gone through drastic shifts

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.120
in intelligence, temperament, and physical
power.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:34.240
He's been one of Marvel's most powerful heroes,
and he's also been one of its dumbest.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:39.180
He's a character who has literally lived many
lives, so the fact that the Drax of the movies

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.560
feels like a completely different person is
in keeping with a long tradition of re-invention.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.100
From his quest for vengeance against Thanos
to his surprising connection to the planet

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.600
Earth, here is everything you need to know
about Drax the Destroyer.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.740
"Nothing goes over my head.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.800
My reflexes are too fast.

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:57.480
I would catch it."

00:00:58.440 --> 00:00:59.220
Where I'm from

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:05.420
Drax's origin story appeared in 1974's Captain
Marvel #32, written by Jim Starlin.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:10.180
In the issue, readers learn about the hero's
homeworld, and it's the last place you'd expect:

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.100
Earth.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.560
As originally written by Starlin, Drax was
a human being by the name of Arthur Douglas,

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.020
who had a wife named Yvette and a daughter,
Heather.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.400
During Thanos' first scouting mission to Earth,
Arthur and his family had the bad luck to

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.600
be on the road in the Nevada desert as the
Titan flew by in his ship.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.580
Thanos attacked, fatally wounding Arthur and
Yvette.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.460
Unbeknownst to anyone, Heather escaped — but
we'll have more to say about her later.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:37.000
After the incident, Thanos' father Mentor
called out to Chronos, father of the gods,

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.760
for help in stopping his wayward son.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.720
Chronos obliged Mentor and built a super powerful
body, which he used as a vessel for Arthur's

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:44.220
soul.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.840
Arthur Douglas may have been no more, but
his soul and sense of vengeance lived on in

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.060
a new form: Drax.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:53.400
It's a vastly different origin story in the
MCU.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.700
In Guardians of the Galaxy, Drax's comic book
origins as a human man are completely ignored.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:03.560
Instead of Yvette and Heather, he had a wife
named Hovat and a daughter named Kamaria.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.280
Both of them met their ends thanks to Ronan
the Accuser, acting on orders from Thanos.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:09.520
"What were they like?"

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.600
"My wife and daughter?"

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.420
"They were kind, brave, true."

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.040
The rewrite of the origin story is a simple
but effective change.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:25.790
The movie version keeps Drax's thirst for
vengeance, just without the complicated wrinkle

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:27.820
of extraterrestrial reincarnation.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:30.260
"I kind of feel like Drax is now mine."

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.220
Power levels

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:36.520
As far as his strength is concerned, the Drax
of the movies is fairly middle-tier.

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:40.599
You certainly wouldn't want to arm wrestle
him, but he also better not get on the Hulk's

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.280
bad side.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.780
That wasn't always the case, as the Drax of
the comics has occasionally been one of Marvel's

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.280
most powerful heroes.

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:52.859
The Destroyer has regularly held his own against
the absolute A-list of Marvel tough guys including

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.240
Thor, the Silver Surfer, and the Hulk.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.030
Along with having a lot more strength, the
Drax of the comics used to have the power

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:02.900
of flight regularly flying through space without
a helmet or space suit.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:06.860
He also had the ability to fire powerful energy
blasts from his hands.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:12.020
The Drax of the panels became more like what
we see in the movies in 2005's Drax the Destroyer

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:12.520
miniseries.

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:18.260
After having one body destroyed in the second
issue, Drax was reborn smaller and less physically

00:03:18.269 --> 00:03:22.579
powerful, but with a much greater degree of
intelligence than the vengeance-driven brute

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:23.340
he used to be.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.500
Bring me Thanos

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:30.740
Even though destroying Thanos is Drax's sole
purpose, he hasn't proven himself to be particularly

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.700
good at his job.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:36.380
In Drax's earliest appearances, his obsession
with Thanos is so intense that he can be as

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:39.120
much of a liability to the heroes on his side
as a help.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:44.620
He cares little about plans, schemes, or strategies
he simply throws himself at the Mad Titan.

00:03:45.129 --> 00:03:50.460
When he reappeared after a long absence in
1990's Silver Surfer #37, he attacked everyone

00:03:50.469 --> 00:03:54.660
in sight, screaming "Where's Thanos?" over
and over, not listening or caring about the

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:56.060
fact that no one knew the answer.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:02.209
In 2006's Annihilation #4, after over three
decades of trying and failing, Drax finally

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:04.500
managed to exact his vengeance against Thanos.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:08.900
Naturally, he just had to do it while Thanos
was trying to save the galaxy during one of

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:10.360
his rare good guy turns.

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:15.300
As Thanos works to stop the villain Annihilus
from destroying all life in the universe,

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:20.060
Drax decides his vengeance is more important,
and punches Thanos' heart out of his chest.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.919
Sure, the timing of it was pretty bad, but
you can't blame a guy for doing what he was

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:24.600
born to do.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.180
My daughter, Moondragon

00:04:27.620 --> 00:04:31.530
In the comics, Drax eventually learns that
his daughter Heather survived the attack in

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:32.030
the desert.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:36.560
Rescued by Thanos' father Mentor, Heather
was brought to Titan and raised there by a

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.180
group of powerful monks, where she developed
the powers of a superhero, taking on the name

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:41.680
Moondragon.

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:46.160
Though Moondragon would eventually join the
Avengers, the Defenders, the Infinity Watch,

00:04:46.169 --> 00:04:50.560
and even the Guardians of the Galaxy, she
didn't always share the more heroic values

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:51.540
of her comrades.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.800
Sometimes, she acted downright evil.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:58.520
While traveling through space with Drax, she
came across a planet immersed in war, and

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.120
solved the problem by mentally enslaving all
the inhabitants.

00:05:01.560 --> 00:05:05.640
To help persuade his daughter to take another
course of action, Drax contacted the Avengers

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:06.140
for help.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.940
Along with a mind-controlled Thor, Moondragon
fought against Drax, and succeeded in defeating

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:11.440
him.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.600
It was the ultimate injustice — he was felled
by his own daughter, and didn't even really

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:16.100
deserve it.

00:05:16.610 --> 00:05:17.900
"You people have issues."

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:19.500
"Of course I have issues!

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.940
That's my freakin' father!"

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.800
As you might imagine, Drax and Moondragon's
relationship has been pretty strained ever

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:27.300
since.

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:29.280
The idiot

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:34.540
When Drax returned to life in Silver Surfer
#35, his mind wasn't fully healed.

00:05:34.880 --> 00:05:39.880
Though still intent on securing Thanos' destruction,
the intergalactic warrior came back a little

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.280
more lovable and a whole, whole lot dumber.

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:46.880
Drax's diminished IQ was used for comedic
purposes, with his brute strength and odd

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:48.740
passions being mined for laughs.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:54.340
When Adam Warlock arrives to recruit Drax
for a new team, Drax is busy smashing TV monitors

00:05:54.340 --> 00:05:58.540
because he's angry the transmission of the
earth show Alf has been interrupted.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:02.759
Drax's mind didn't stay dull forever, but
his intelligence wasn't restored fully in

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:06.759
a way that stuck until 2005's Drax the Destroyer
miniseries.

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:10.840
No matter what intelligence level he's been
at, though, he's always remembered how to

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:11.840
play a mean sax.

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:14.520
A cosmic custodian

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:18.920
The conclusion of Infinity Gauntlet story
left the Gauntlet and its six gems under the

00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:20.420
guardianship of Adam Warlock.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:24.540
Marvel's cosmic pantheon wasn't happy with
this arrangement, however, and encouraged

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:25.700
him to share the burden.

00:06:26.140 --> 00:06:30.700
Keeping the soul gem for himself, Adam chose
five people to be the guardians of the remaining

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.540
gems, creating a team known as the Infinity
Watch.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:37.380
Warlock would later wonder if he had made
the right decisions with the people he chose

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:42.060
to carry the gems, fearing the influence of
the Infinity Gauntlet had corrupted his judgment.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.220
It's no surprise why he thought this.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:48.880
He gave the space gem to the mischievous Pip
the Troll, who immediately used it to steal,

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.020
among other things, an Avengers quinjet.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:55.970
The mind gem went to Moondragon, a woman you'll
recall once used her powers to enslave an

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:56.780
entire world.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.500
The reality gem went to Thanos, of all people.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:04.220
Finally, Adam gave the power gem to Drax,
the dimwitted brute who destroys things when

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:05.760
he misses an episode of Alf.

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:07.160
Good leadership, Adam.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:09.520
Famously huge

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:14.330
The movie Drax is an alien, while the comic
book Drax is an earthling who was forced into

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.420
a constructed body.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:18.940
This naturally means there are a number of
differences between them.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:20.860
One of the more surprising differences?

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:21.620
Well.

00:07:21.660 --> 00:07:25.980
There's a specific bodily function comic book
Drax doesn't have to worry about.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:30.400
In the beginning of Guardians of the Galaxy
Vol. 2, Rocket threatens to fill up Peter

00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:34.300
Quill's pillow with fecal matter while he
sleeps, because that's the kind of mature

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:36.250
and responsible team that the Guardians are..

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:38.800
"You put your turd in my bed I'll shave you."

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:40.960
"Oh it won't be my turd.

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:41.720
It'll be Drax's."

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.240
"Hahaha.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:46.540
I have famously huge turds."

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.800
Believe it or not, this is an invention specific
to the movies.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:54.040
In the comics, the size of Drax's bowel movements
isn't any sort of legend.

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:56.380
As it turns out, he doesn't have them at all.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:01.520
In Warlock &amp; the Infinity Watch #2, when Adam
Warlock gives Drax the power gem, Drax doesn't

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:02.740
know what to do with it.

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:05.540
Thinking he's been handed a jelly bean, he
promptly eats it.

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:10.800
Understandably, Gamora freaks out, and Warlock
tries to reassure her, reminding her that

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.020
the gem is indestructible and won't digest.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:18.820
When she continues to protest, Warlock says,
"Drax's physical being is unlike most creatures.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:19.900
I'll explain later.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.420
Trust me, he won't lose it."

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:24.440
In other words, the Drax of the comic books
doesn't poop.

00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:27.080
No wonder he seems so much happier in the
movies.

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:28.440
Thanks for watching!

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.819
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:30.819 --> 00:08:32.790
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

